course: dictionary
lesson: 12214
title: Making a conjecture
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A conjecture is a guess that someone makes when they do not have all the facts yet. «I think the match was cancelled, since the pitch looks flooded.» The speaker has not seen an official message, so this is a conjecture, not a sure fact.
explain: The word works as a noun and as a verb. «Her conjecture was that the lost cat had gone home.» Here conjecture is the guess itself. «We conjectured that the bridge was closed» uses it as a verb: we guessed it, because of what we saw.
explain: Words like «guess», «suppose», «I think», «perhaps» and «not sure» are clues that a conjecture is coming. «It is pure conjecture, because nobody has seen the evidence» tells you the guess has no proof behind it at all.
explain: In maths, a conjecture is a statement that mathematicians believe is true but have not yet proved. «Every even number greater than 2 is the sum of two prime numbers» is a famous conjecture. People have checked it with very large numbers, but nobody has yet proved it for every even number.
fact: A conjecture is a guess or opinion formed without full proof.
fact: To conjecture means to guess or suppose something when you do not have all the facts.
fact: «Pure conjecture» means a guess with no real evidence behind it.
fact: In maths, a conjecture is a statement mathematicians believe is true but have not yet proved.
fact: Once a conjecture is proved, it is no longer just a conjecture.
exercise: «The detective made a conjecture about who took the painting, but she had no proof yet.» What is a conjecture here? | A list of everyone in the room | A dance from long ago | A fact checked by three witnesses | *A guess made without full proof
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to conjecture? | proof | certainty | answer | *guess
exercise: A statement that mathematicians think is true but have not yet proved is called a what? | a riddle | a fact | *a conjecture | a sum
test: Which sentence shows a conjecture? | *«I think the match was cancelled, since the pitch looks flooded.» | «Two plus two is four.» | «The bell rang at nine.»
test: Why is a conjecture not a fact? | Because only grown-ups can make one | Because it is written in a big book | *Because it is a guess made without full proof | Because it is always wrong
exam: Which is the best meaning of conjecture in maths? | A rule that has been proved for ever | *A statement believed to be true but not yet proved | A number that cannot be divided by any other number | A picture of a triangle
